"{\"requirement\": \"The modern armchair has a rounded, ergonomic design with a slightly depressed seat cushion for comfort. The backrest curves smoothly for support, and the armrests are short and curved, positioned for elbow rest. Four straight, square wooden legs provide a stable base. The chair features nailhead trim along the bottom front edge, adding a decorative and functional element. The upholstery is a smooth, durable fabric, likely tweed or linen, in a solid gray color. The chair is symmetrical and presented against a plain black background.\", \"articulation_required\": false, \"plan\": {\"object_name\": \"Modern rounded upholstered armchair\", \"components\": [{\"name\": \"seat_base\", \"description\": \"Primary upholstered seat/body foundation, centered at the origin and symmetric about x=0. Use a broad rounded-rectangle footprint, approximately 1.6 times as wide as it is deep and about 0.20–0.25 of chair height thick. The front faces -y. Its front edge is gently convex in plan, side edges taper slightly narrower toward +y, and all vertical edges are strongly rounded. Construct with local hulls between rounded primitives or a linear_extrude of a sampled rounded profile; preserve a soft upholstered silhouette rather than a sharp box.\"}, {\"name\": \"seat_cushion\", \"description\": \"Thick removable-looking cushion placed above the seat base. Dominant outline is a rounded trapezoid: broad across x, slightly narrower toward the back (+y), with a softly bowed front edge. Cross-section has a domed perimeter and a shallow central depression for an ergonomic, sat-in appearance; the top slopes subtly downward toward the center while the lower face remains nearly level. Approximate the soft form using hulls of flattened spheres or rounded solids, with a shallow boolean_difference depression if needed. Cushion width should fit between the armrests with narrow gaps, and cushion thickness should be about one quarter of its depth.\"}, {\"name\": \"backrest\", \"description\": \"Upholstered back rising from the rear of the seat at +y. It has a wide, continuous rounded outline with low rounded shoulders near the armrests and a gently arched upper edge. In side profile, the backrest leans slightly rearward toward +y as it rises and curves concavely toward the sitter on its front face, providing lumbar and upper-back support. Thickness is greatest near the lower attachment and tapers modestly upward. Form with several vertically arranged rounded sections joined by hull, or a sampled side/profile extrusion, avoiding a flat slab appearance.\"}, {\"name\": \"left_armrest\", \"description\": \"Short upholstered arm on the -x side, attached to the seat base and lower backrest. It begins near the front half of the seat, rises to elbow height, and sweeps upward and rearward into the backrest. Dominant side outline is a low curved wedge with a rounded top rail; cross-section is thick and softly oval/rounded rectangular. The inner face slightly cups the seat, while the outer face is smoothly convex. Build from local hulls between rounded primitives. It must not extend as far forward as the seat cushion front.\"}, {\"name\": \"right_armrest\", \"description\": \"Mirror of the left armrest on the +x side. Maintain identical height, length, thickness, curvature, and attachment geometry. Its rounded upper surface supports the elbow and transitions continuously into the lower side of the backrest.\"}, {\"name\": \"front_left_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square-section wooden leg beneath the front-left corner (-x,-y). Slender vertical or with only a very slight outward splay, with crisp planar faces and subtly eased edges. Height is approximately 0.28–0.33 of total chair height; square width is about 0.12–0.16 of leg height. Use a Cube with warm medium-to-dark wood appearance.\"}, {\"name\": \"front_right_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the front-right corner (+x,-y), mirrored from the front-left leg. Match section, height, finish, and any slight splay.\"}, {\"name\": \"rear_left_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the rear-left corner (-x,+y). It may sit slightly farther inward or be partially obscured by the upholstered body, but must visibly contact and support the seat base. Match the front legs in material and section.\"}, {\"name\": \"rear_right_leg\", \"description\": \"Straight square wooden leg beneath the rear-right corner (+x,+y), mirrored from the rear-left leg and matching all other legs in finish and scale.\"}, {\"name\": \"nailhead_trim\", \"description\": \"Single evenly spaced row of small metallic hemispherical or shallow round nailheads following the lower front edge of the upholstered seat base. Arrange symmetrically across x, just above the leg attachment level on the -y face. Use repeated small spheres or short cylinders; spacing should be roughly 1.5–2 nailhead diameters, with the end nailheads inset equally from both front corners. The row may follow a slight convex front arc rather than remaining perfectly straight.\"}, {\"name\": \"upholstery_finish\", \"description\": \"Unified smooth, durable solid-gray tweed or linen appearance applied to the seat base, cushion, backrest, and armrests. Keep the modeled surface largely matte with very subtle fabric character; avoid bold patterns, seams, tufting, or high gloss.\"}, {\"name\": \"presentation_background\", \"description\": \"Plain black presentation ground/background, visually separate from the chair. If scene geometry is required, use a large matte black rear plane and optional floor plane without visible texture or distracting edges.\"}], \"relations\": [\"Coordinate convention: +x is chair right, +y is toward the rear/inward, +z is upward; the chair front therefore faces -y.\", \"The complete chair is bilaterally symmetric about the vertical yz plane at x=0, except for negligible fabric irregularity that need not be modeled.\", \"The seat base is the main structural hub: all four legs attach beneath it, the cushion rests on it, and the armrests and backrest grow from its side and rear perimeter.\", \"The seat cushion is centered laterally between the arms, sits directly on the seat base, and leaves only narrow side and rear reveal gaps; its depressed center remains above the surrounding support structure.\", \"The backrest joins the rear (+y) of the seat base without a large opening and curves forward toward the occupant while leaning slightly rearward overall.\", \"Both armrests are lower than the backrest top, approximately level with the lower third to middle of the backrest, and blend into the backrest at their rear ends.\", \"The armrests terminate behind the cushion's foremost edge, keeping the chair visually open at the front.\", \"The front legs sit beneath the left and right front corners, spaced symmetrically around x=0; the rear legs repeat this stable rectangular support layout toward +y.\", \"All four leg bottoms are coplanar on the floor, and each leg top penetrates or directly contacts the underside of the seat base with no floating gaps.\", \"The nailhead trim is attached to the upholstered lower front fascia, above and between the front legs, and follows the front edge at a constant offset.\", \"Upholstered forms use coordinated rounded transitions, while the legs deliberately contrast through straight square geometry and a wood material.\", \"The chair should be isolated and centered against the black background, with enough contrast that the gray upholstery, wooden legs, and metallic nailheads remain distinguishable.\"], \"critic_checklist\": [\"Verify exact bilateral symmetry of the major chair silhouette, cushion, armrests, backrest, legs, and nailhead layout about x=0.\", \"Confirm the chair reads as an armchair rather than a dining chair: broad upholstered seat, integrated short arms, substantial curved back, and four exposed legs.\", \"Check that the seat cushion has a visible but shallow central depression; it must not appear flat, deeply bowl-shaped, or collapsed.\", \"Check that the cushion outline is softly rounded and slightly narrower toward +y, with a gently bowed front edge facing -y.\", \"Verify that the backrest is smoothly curved in both front view and side profile, with rounded shoulders and no sharp slab-like corners.\", \"Ensure the backrest supports the full seat width but remains proportionally taller than the armrests and does not become an oversized wingback.\", \"Confirm each armrest is short, rounded, suitable for elbow support, and ends behind the front edge of the cushion.\", \"Confirm the left and right armrests transition smoothly into the backrest and do not visibly float above the seat body.\", \"Verify all four legs are present, straight, square in cross-section, equal in section and compatible in height, with only subtle optional splay.\", \"Check that all leg bottoms share one floor plane and that the seat base is level and stably supported.\", \"Ensure the wooden legs contrast clearly with the gray upholstery but do not dominate the upholstered body.\", \"Verify the nailheads form one clean, evenly spaced, centered row along the lower front edge; reject missing, irregular, oversized, or asymmetrical studs.\", \"Ensure nailheads are small metallic raised elements, not holes, buttons, tufting, or a continuous rail.\", \"Check for a cohesive solid-gray upholstery treatment across cushion, body, arms, and back; avoid color blocking, strong patterns, leather gloss, or visible tufting.\", \"Confirm rounded upholstery edges remain soft but controlled, without lumpy hull artifacts, accidental concavities, Boolean tears, or intersections.\", \"Check that the front is consistently oriented toward -y and the trim and front legs are on that side.\", \"Verify the final silhouette has balanced proportions: width greater than depth, seat height below the midpoint of total height, and backrest forming the tallest element.\", \"Confirm the background is plain black and visually separate from the modeled chair, with no distracting props or scenery.\"]}, \"assignment\": \"Write source.py with the complete initial implementation.\"}"
